{
  "description": "Cross-language conformance fixture for a load run's verdict (issues #3537, #3538). Read by the engine gtest suite (engine/tests/run_export_test.cpp, via VAYU_ENGINE_SOURCE_DIR, through the run-report export's `verdict` and the Markdown/HTML verdict line) and by the app's vitest suite (app/src/components/shared/run-outcome.test.ts, through `reportOutcome`). Each case's `report` is a GET /runs/:runId/report answer cut to what a verdict reads - `metadata.status`, `summary.totalRequests` and `summary.errorRate`, `summary.drainCut.cancelled` (the requests a Stop cut from the drain of a run that ended on its own, issue #3538; a load row carries it as `resultSummary.drainCut.cancelled`), `thresholdValidation` and the top-level `assertions` block - plus the sections that block summarises (`scenario`, `testValidation`, `elements`, `lifecycle`), kept consistent with it so a reader that re-derives a failed check from them instead of reading the block answers differently on some case. `expected.state` is the export's `verdict.state` (`not_judged` is the app's `not-judged`); `expected.reason` is the export's `verdict.reason`; `expected.names` are the phrases the verdict's words must contain, in this order, on every surface: the export's Markdown and HTML line and the app's not-judged reason. The error-rate phrase is each surface's own and is never listed. A case with no `names` must name no failed check. A report stored before the block carries one derived from what it stored (GET /runs/:runId/report, `assertions`); the `old run` cases are those reports.",
